The goal is not to remove every advanced feature. Keep advanced forensic capabilities that map to the SRS, but stop displaying them as always-active decorative widgets when the underlying system is not connected.
Remove from production or make clearly sandbox-only
- Fake demo samples/results mixed into real dashboard and case screens.
- Randomly generated case/evidence/certificate IDs.
- Decorative pipeline stages that progress without a server job.
- Fake test-tampering flow on real evidence. If kept, place it in an isolated developer sandbox with a prominent “synthetic test only” label and no writes to real records.
- Fake biometric camera/verification, generated signatures, mock certificate IDs and fake ledger/chain claims.
- Repeated “security-grade / court-ready / immutable / certified” claims without implemented proof and approved wording.
- Repeated animated waveforms/spectrograms that are not linked to selected audio or actual analysis.
- Auto-playing or generated narration presented as the evidence recording. Keep screen-reader labels or optional UI narration separate from original-audio playback.
Consolidate or demote to secondary navigation
- Avoid several separate screens that repeat the same evidence details without adding a distinct user task. Prefer one Evidence Detail page with tabs: Overview, Deepfake Analysis, Explainability, Integrity, Speaker Verification, Voice Condition/Disguise, Reviews, and Custody.
- Keep the case list and case detail as the main workflow; place model comparison and model configuration under Admin/Model Management.
- Keep public report verification separate from internal evidence management; public view must reveal only approved public metadata.
- Keep Workflow as a concise “How analysis works / system status” page, not another dashboard that repeats the same pipeline cards.
- Avoid multiple export buttons for formats that are not genuinely implemented. Offer PDF only until another format has real generation and tests.
- Move advanced ML metrics, thresholds, raw model outputs and technical signal plots into expandable “Technical details” sections. The main result should state the verdict/status, confidence only if returned and calibrated, a plain-language explanation, limitations and expert review state.
- Avoid too many large gauges, radar charts, decorative percentages, duplicate summary cards and redundant status chips. They increase visual noise and make the app feel less trustworthy.
Recommended main navigation
1. Overview — real counts, recent activity, queue/service status; clear empty state.
2. Cases — create, search/filter, open, edit/close.
3. Evidence — case-scoped uploads and integrity state.
