5. Expert Review — pending findings, validation/dispute/needs-review, reasoned override.
6. Reports — genuine report generation and verification.
7. Audit & Custody — real server records.
8. Notifications — persisted read/unread state.
9. Administration — users, model registry, thresholds, deployment status.
10. Settings — only settings that are actually saved and supported.
Role-based access should hide unavailable navigation items, but the server must still enforce authorization. Do not create a separate navigation item for every small feature if it can be grouped naturally under the selected case/evidence.
